  "worked_solution": "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base.\n\nTo do this, we write $125$ as ${5}^{3},$ and then rewrite the right-hand side using the power rule of exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{m-10} & ={125}^{m} \\\\ {5}^{m-10} & ={({5}^{3})}^{m} \\\\ {5}^{m-10} & ={5}^{3m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m-10 & =3m \\\\ -2m & =10 \\\\ m & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
